Subject: [PATCH] Construct GPU broadcast inference results directly

The pinned GCC 16.2.1 build diagnoses free-nonheap-object in the move
assignment that replaces a preinitialized vector<PartialShape>. That vector
is discarded in either constant-target branch. Return each branch result
from an immediately invoked lambda so the output vector is initialized
once. Preserve shape inference, memory-lock scopes, format selection and
the dynamic-shape fallback. All warning and optimization flags remain.

--- a/src/plugins/intel_gpu/src/graph/broadcast.cpp
+++ b/src/plugins/intel_gpu/src/graph/broadcast.cpp
@@ -59,7 +59,6 @@
 
     ShapeType pattern_shape = impl_param.input_layouts.size() == 2 ? impl_param.get_input_layout(1).get<ShapeType>()
                                                                    : ShapeType(ov::Shape{ target_shape.size() });
-    std::vector<ShapeType> output_shapes = {ShapeType{}};
     std::vector<ShapeType> input_shapes = {
         input0_layout.get<ShapeType>(),
         pattern_shape
@@ -77,25 +76,28 @@
         const_data.emplace(2, axes_mapping_tensor);
     }
 
